"""DSpark MTP draft model for DeepSeek-V4-Flash-DSpark — faithful port of the
reference block-parallel drafter (checkpoint ``inference/model.py``).

Reference algorithm (DSparkBlock / Transformer.forward_spec):
  * main_x = main_norm(main_proj(concat of target-layer [40,41,42] hiddens)).
  * Draft block = [anchor_token, noise x4] (dspark_block_size=5) embedded and
    HC-expanded; ALL 3 mtp blocks run sequentially in ONE pass over the block.
  * Each block's DSparkAttention: 5 block queries attend a per-request sliding
    WINDOW (128) of past main_kv (one entry per target position, slot=pos%128)
    plus the 5 block kv entries (non-causal within block), with attn_sink in
    the softmax denominator, MQA over a single 512-dim latent kv.
  * Output head: hc_head collapse -> RMSNorm -> tied lm_head, then an
    AUTOREGRESSIVE markov-correction loop: logits[:,i] += markov_head(prev
    drafted token), sample, repeat.

vLLM proposer integration ("stash" scheme): the generic proposer calls the
drafter K times, 1 token/step.  At spec step 0 we run the ENTIRE block draft
(insert main_kv for every accepted-token row, then one block-parallel pass)
and stash the 5 markov-corrected per-position logits; steps 1..K-1 are no-op
replays that return the stashed logits column by column.  Greedy draft
sampling in the proposer then reproduces the reference markov chain exactly.
Drafter output only affects the speculative ACCEPTANCE RATE — the target
model verifies every token, so any drafter deficiency degrades speed, never
correctness.

Checkpoint weights live under ``mtp.{i}.*``; block sub-weights map to
``mtp_blocks.{i}.*`` (DeepseekV4DecoderLayer), DSpark-specific weights stay at
the layer top level.
"""

